        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets the Direction Cosine Matrix (DCM) for the <ref refid="structastrea_1_1astro_1_1frames_1_1Perifocal" kindref="compound">Perifocal</ref> frame at a given date. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the specific angular momentum vector (h = r x v, giving the W axis) and the eccentricity vector (e = (v x h) / mu - r_hat, giving the P axis, i.e. the direction to periapsis), then completes the right-handed triad with Q = W x P.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>date</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The date for which the DCM is requested. Unused: the perifocal frame&apos;s orientation only depends on the (unperturbed) orbital plane and periapsis location, not on the current date. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>DirectionCosineMatrix&lt;parent, Perifocal&gt; The DCM from parent to <ref refid="structastrea_1_1astro_1_1frames_1_1Perifocal" kindref="compound">Perifocal</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
